The pinned upstream tree has no separate NOTICE file. This document is a
local provenance record, not a NOTICE supplied by upstream. The repository's
MIT-0 license does not replace the Apache-2.0 license for this vendored code.

Local modifications
-------------------
The ProveIt port adapts Lean 4.34.1 / Mathlib d13f23b7 source to this
workspace's Lean 4.32.0 / Mathlib v4.32.0. Modified upstream files carry
"Modified for ProveIt" notices describing their changes. Local compatibility
declarations are in lean/OAI/Compat/. FreimanAffineBox.lean is an explicitly
marked extract of upstream NativeProperAffineRecovery.lean. Its two theorem
statements and proof bodies are retained in the distinct
OAI.Erdos3.FreimanModel.ProveItExtract namespace to avoid collisions with
the originals when both import paths meet. Local additions
and modifications in this directory are also distributed under Apache-2.0.
Results/Conclusions.lean and Estimates/UniformRelativePatchSource.lean are
density-only extracts of the corresponding files at the same pinned revision.
They omit the reciprocal-sum branch, which the Gowers formalization does not
use. Their original source hashes remain in the manifest; omission does not
alter the license or copyright status of the retained material.

README.md describes the verified subset and the quantitative port still in
progress. quantitative-port-manifest.json records the pinned quantitative
import closure and SHA-256 hashes of the original upstream files. Git
history records local changes; these changes do not imply upstream
endorsement or verification of the port.

Additional Mathlib backport
--------------------------
lean/OAI/Compat/ExteriorPower.lean is ported from Mathlib, rather than from
openai/math. Its original notice is retained verbatim in the source:

Copyright (c) 2026 Justus Springer. All rights reserved.
Released under Apache 2.0 license as described in the file LICENSE.
Authors: Justus Springer

Repository: https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4
Revision: d13f23b723b8a846827a245b89c10fc7d3f11612
Original path: Mathlib/Analysis/InnerProductSpace/ExteriorPower.lean
Pinned source:
https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/d13f23b723b8a846827a245b89c10fc7d3f11612/Mathlib/Analysis/InnerProductSpace/ExteriorPower.lean

LICENSE.mathlib reproduces the license file from that Mathlib revision
unchanged. The port retains the original copyright and author header,
records its modifications prominently, and keeps the original source hash
in quantitative-port-manifest.json. Its local module path is changed to
OAI.Compat.ExteriorPower to work with the older workspace toolchain.

Gowers polynomial partition adaptation outside this directory
-------------------------------------------------------------
Combinatorics/Ramsey/Lean/GowersSzemeredi/Proofs05MinimumPolynomialPartition.lean
adapts PolynomialCoordinatePartitionBound and its induction from the pinned
Polynomial/PolynomialCoordinatePartition.lean source. It strengthens the cell
length guarantee using comparable residue progressions and changes the
induction scale and degree-dependent exponent. Its prominent source notice
and adjacent LICENSE.openai-math retain provenance, copyright attribution,
and the full Apache-2.0 license. This is a consumer of the existing port;
it introduces no additional upstream module into the vendored closure.

Gowers robust-difference adaptation outside this directory
--------------------------------------------------------
Combinatorics/Ramsey/Lean/GowersSzemeredi/Proofs16RobustDifferenceBohr.lean
adapts the width/rank calculation of exists_quartic_bogolyubov from the
pinned Estimates/LocalizedSiftingAlmostPeriods.lean source. It changes the
error to 1/4, retains the pointwise estimate for an arbitrary difference
event, and supplies robust four-term counts via popular differences.
The companion Proofs16RobustDifferenceProgression.lean adapts the
progression extraction from exists_quartic_bogolyubov_progression to retain
uniform representation counts. Their prominent source notices and adjacent
LICENSE.openai-math retain provenance, copyright attribution and full
Apache-2.0 terms. They consume an existing selected port module; no upstream
module is added to the closure.
